      "writtenOn": "2019-08-28T18:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CONFIG_HAS_MATRIX_KEYBOARD looks to me more clear and intuitive than CONFIG_NO_MATRIX_KEYBOARD. I think it\u0027s less readable to double-negate in general. In this case, the code would look: !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NO_MATRIX_KEYBOARD). One of my favorite examples is:\n\n  batt_disconnect_status !\u003d BATTERY_NOT_DISCONNECTED\n\nThe following is more readable:\n\n  batt_connect_status \u003d\u003d BATTERY_DISCONNECTED\n\nWhat names are available depends on the context but in the case of CONFIG_HAS_MATRIX_KEYBOARD, I think we don\u0027t need to negate the name.",
      "parentUuid": "68e4302e_1cb4bb83",
